  "query_preview": "..The high to our east begins to move westward and \nstrengthen today and through the weekend. This slowly introduces \ndrier, mid-level air and subsidence, activity will slow down. We \ndon't expect a total stop, but it will be slow through the weekend. \nThe high may return to a more favorable location by next week, with \neasterly steering flow returning, but much can change in a week and \nwe will see.\n\nAdditionally, once the high relocates and strengthens, along with \nthe Monsoon pause/slow down, temperatures will soar. We expect many \nareas to reach the warmest readings so far this year. The various \nheat products that have been issued remain appropriate.",
